Z||000000||86SE||01-14-2000||11:20 PM||||I was driving my 86 V-6 back to south dakota from Niobrara, NE back in August when I watched as the odometer changed from 84999 to 85000, no more than 5 seconds after it turned, BOOM!! then RPM dropped to 0000, so I pulled it over popped the deck lid and a spark plug wire fell off the plug!! I waited a while B4 I put it back on and then started it up and my exhaust is LOUD!!, it sounds like a leak right under the cat. converter...  Is is the cat. converter that would get a hole blown in it, or the muffler??||||reg||8
Z||000001||Sage||01-15-2000||12:49 AM||||If the converter was plugged, it needed to "relieve" the preassure, so it picked a weak spot and popped it out!  Could have seperated the pipe that goes into the converter from it.||||reg||5
Z||000002||DXR_DAD||01-15-2000||01:03 AM||||86SE It sounds like it's time for a new exhaust system(complete) I did mine (complete) New Ported and Re-weld Manifolds, cat. muffler, pipes and tips all under $800.00. I didn't want to waste any time with the whole thing so I replaced all if it. I have read that the the manifolds can re crack after the weld?? but also I know people that have fixed a crack more than once.  I would say I you have the $$$ replace with New parts!!!||||reg||1
Z||000003||batboy||01-15-2000||08:30 AM||||What happened when the plug wire fell off was that raw gas from the dead cylinder washed down into the exhaust system and eventually exploded. Probably in the head pipe or cat area. It's muffler shop time.||||reg||1
